{"text":" In 1803, the United States doubled in size. Over night, it paid about $3.8. In 1867, it bottled land more than twice the size of Texas. People called it a folly. And in 1946, it secretly tried to buy the biggest island on Earth, with gold. $828,000 square miles for $15 million, about $3 cents an acre. Alaska is more than twice the size of Texas. Newspapers called it Sewer's Icebox. Some even called it Walruscia. The price, $25 million in gold, for about $134 square miles. That's almost $300 an acre, compared to Louisiana, about 10,000 times more expensive. And the answer from Denmark and Greenland was the same. Greenland is not for sale. Which deal would you have made? And should America still try to buy Greenland? Tell me in the comments.","chunks":[{"text":" In","timestamp":[0.24,0.7]},{"text":" 1803,","timestamp":[0.7,1.42]},{"text":" the","timestamp":[1.6,1.8]},{"text":" United","timestamp":[1.8,2.1]},{"text":" States","timestamp":[2.1,2.66]},{"text":" doubled","timestamp":[2.66,2.9]},{"text":" in","timestamp":[2.9,3.22]},{"text":" size.","timestamp":[3.22,3.76]},{"text":" Over","timestamp":[4.06,4.32]},{"text":" night,","timestamp":[4.32,4.92]},{"text":" it","timestamp":[5.06,5.22]},{"text":" paid","timestamp":[5.22,5.44]},{"text":" about","timestamp":[5.44,5.76]},{"text":" $3","timestamp":[5.76,6.12]},{"text":".8.","timestamp":[6.12,6.68]},{"text":" In","timestamp":[7.18,7.48]},{"text":" 1867,","timestamp":[7.48,8.36]},{"text":" it","timestamp":[8.68,8.88]},{"text":" bottled","timestamp":[8.88,9.18]},{"text":" land","timestamp":[9.18,9.38]},{"text":" more","timestamp":[9.38,9.52]},{"text":" than","timestamp":[9.52,9.96]},{"text":" twice","timestamp":[9.96,10.22]},{"text":" the","timestamp":[10.22,10.44]},{"text":" size","timestamp":[10.44,10.6]},{"text":" of","timestamp":[10.6,10.9]},{"text":" Texas.","timestamp":[10.9,11.52]},{"text":" People","timestamp":[11.82,12.08]},{"text":" called","timestamp":[12.08,12.24]},{"text":" it","timestamp":[12.24,12